// package wj: the Odin side of Wren's JavaScript glue — the one shared helper layer every ported domain imports.
//
// This is the Odin equivalent of native/js/engine/wj.h + qjs_backend.h + the parts of native/js/runtime/web.h that a
// ported domain uses. A domain written in Odin (native/js/odin/web_*.odin, dom_*.odin, ...) imports this package
// instead of including those headers; the whole lot is compiled to one wasm32 object (odin build native/js/odin) and
// linked by zig's wasm-ld with the QuickJS-ng objects and the remaining C glue into the one engine module, exactly as
// native/js/odin_spike proved. See docs/js/odin-glue.md for the rules (where a new helper goes, how to declare an
// import, how to add a domain, and how the G1/G4 agents rebase onto this unified layer).
//
// ONE declaration per symbol. The layer used to be a wj.odin plus a wj_gN.odin per porting agent (and wr_g1.odin,
// wjd_g1.odin, three C shims), each redeclaring the QuickJS API, the wj_*/web_* functions and the wr_* imports it
// happened to need; that collided ("Redeclaration of ...") the moment they were compiled together. Now, by theme:
//
//   wj.odin         this file: the package doc and the core opaque types (JSValue, Context, Runtime, the proc shapes).
//   quickjs.odin    the QuickJS-ng public C API (quickjs.h JS_EXTERN) as `foreign`, plus the `static inline`
//                   constructors / predicates of quickjs.h reimplemented on the NAN box (no symbol to link to).
//   engine.odin     the engine's C structs mirrored field for field (wj_obj, wj_realm, wj_interface, wj_listener,
//                   wj_buf), its globals (wj_the_realm, wj_scratch...), and the inlines over them (wj_obj_of...).
//   host.odin       the wj_*/web_* functions of native/js/engine and native/js/runtime that stay C (real symbols).
//   wr_imports.odin the browser's imports (wr_*), GENERATED by src/tools/bindgen from api/*.widl: never typed by hand.
//   strings.odin    Str, the scratch buffer and WJ_FETCH_STRING, the JS-string constructors, cstring helpers.
//   values.odin     promises-as-values, blobs, FormData, Headers, streams, signals, the clone serialiser.
//   errors.odin     the error throwers and the error-as-value constructors.
//   dom.odin        dom_internal.h: dom_impl (mirrored) and the dom_core.c helpers.
//   libc.odin       the libc / libm symbols the glue uses.
//   convert.odin, buffer.odin, promise.odin: helpers of wj.h IMPLEMENTED in Odin (ported from qjs_convert.c, buffer.c,
//                   promise.c) and exported under their C names, so the C that remains links against them.
//
// Four kinds of symbol live in the layer:
//   * a function with a real symbol (JS_EXTERN in quickjs.h, a wj_*/web_* of engine/runtime) -> a `foreign` block;
//     wasm-ld resolves it to the C definition in the same module. Names and signatures match the C exactly.
//   * a browser import (wr_*) -> generated, wr_imports.odin.
//   * a `static inline` / macro of the headers (JS_NewInt32, JS_IsException, the JS_UNDEFINED constant, WJ_FETCH_STRING,
//     wj_obj_of, web_set_impl) -> reimplemented here (a few NAN-box bit operations, or a small proc).
//   * a field of a global C struct (wj_the_realm.protos, wj_obj.impl) -> read in place through the mirrored struct;
//     native/js/odin/wj_shim.c asserts every mirrored offset at compile time (it holds no code).
//
// Nothing here allocates Odin memory or uses `context`: procs are "contextless" and the engine's malloc (shared, in the
// same module) is reached through wj.malloc / wj.free when a domain needs raw memory.
package wj

import jscapi "wb:engine/jscapi"

// ---- core types (qjs_backend.h) ----

// The types of the engine API are defined once, in src/engine/jscapi (the QuickJS C API on the Odin runtime), and
// aliased here for both backends: the layer's `foreign` declarations (QuickJS C) and its jscapi aliases
// (backend_jsrt.odin) then take and return the very same types. See WJ_JSRT in backend.odin.

// On wasm32 QuickJS-ng selects NAN boxing: `typedef uint64_t JSValue` (quickjs.h). Odin passes and returns it in one
// wasm i64, matching the C ABI with no struct-by-value question. A glue proc takes and returns JSValue by value.
JSValue :: jscapi.JSValue
Context :: jscapi.Context   // opaque JSContext; only ever used behind a pointer
Runtime :: jscapi.Runtime   // opaque JSRuntime

// A method / constructor / function: (ctx, this, argc, argv) -> result or EXCEPTION. The exact JSCFunction signature.
Native :: jscapi.Native
// An attribute getter: (ctx, this) -> result.
Getter :: jscapi.Getter
// An attribute setter: (ctx, this, value) -> result (undefined or EXCEPTION).
Setter :: jscapi.Setter

// The browser's own handle types the glue passes around (wren_api.h). WR_ABSENT (an absent optional length) and the
// wr_* types come with the generated imports (wr_imports.odin).
Handle :: u64        // wr_Object / a node / a port end; 0 is "none"
